    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d441">

                <pb facs="0479" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/96</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gonzales</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-09T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 9, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 2, 1 p.m.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d441-f1"/> Ships in question should be
                    turned over to the United States Shipping Board to be operated by it with the
                    other tonnage under its control. Shipping Board requests detailed <pb
                        facs="0480" n="308" xml:id="pg308"/> statement of amount of money paid or
                    contracted for repairs by the Cuban Government and also statement of all other
                    liens against ships in addition to liens of Lykes Brothers. Shipping Board
                    states that when vessels are taken over all proper bills will be met.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d441-f1" n="3" xml:id="d441-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see telegram of June 15, 6 p.m., to the Minister, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg299">p. 299</ref>.</p>
            </note>
